{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch11SYGhhRLy2XoCaAQQo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Even items whose layer-4 output was least perturbed (cos 0.97–0.99) end up at final cos ≈ 0.946, with a systematic score offset of +1.7. So the layer-5 edits are not negligible either. Part of that is the constant offset from removing many GELU-floor neurons, and part may be the three removed heads.\n\nI'll check whether the layer-5 edits hurt within-question ranking on the least-perturbed questions. I'll also re-rank layer-5 neurons by total RMS contribution (mean plus variability, relative to the LayerNorm output scale) instead of within-question variance alone, to avoid the large constant offset.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: (1) on questions least damaged before layer 5, within-q ranking is still mostly intact -> layer-5 damage is mainly an offset; (2) ranking L5 neurons by RMS contribution gives sets with much smaller total perturbation.\nfrom scipy.stats import spearmanr\nqc4=np.array([np.mean([c4[idx[(qi,p)]] for p in range(len(practice[qi]['paragraphs']))]) for qi in range(200)])\nrho_q=np.array([spearmanr([so[idx[(qi,p)]] for p in range(10)],[se[idx[(qi,p)]] for p in range(10)])[0] if len(practice[qi]['paragraphs'])==10 else np.nan for qi in range(200)])\no_q=np.argsort(-qc4)\nfor lo,hi in [(0,40),(40,80),(80,120),(120,160),(160,200)]:\n    s=o_q[lo:hi]; print(f\"questions ranked {lo}-{hi} by intactness (mean L4cos {qc4[s].mean():.3f}): spearman {np.nanmean(rho_q[s]):.3f}\")\nga5=W('bert.encoder.layer.5.attention.output.LayerNorm.weight'); ba5=W('bert.encoder.layer.5.attention.output.LayerNorm.bias')\nref=np.sqrt((ga5**2).sum()+(ba5**2).sum()); print(\"L5 LN_a output scale ref ||x_a|| ~ %.1f\"%ref)\nwn=np.linalg.norm(Wout5,axis=0); rmsA=np.sqrt((a5[inA]**2).mean(0))*wn\noR=np.argsort(rmsA)\nfor k in [400,600,800,1000,1300]:\n    for nm,S in [('RMS',oR[:k]),('var',oA[:k])]:\n        D=a5[:, S]@Wout5[:,S].T   # per-item removed contribution vector (attribution, not a forward pass)\n        print(f\"k={k} {nm}: per-item ||removed|| mean {np.linalg.norm(D,axis=1).mean():.2f} ({100*np.linalg.norm(D,axis=1).mean()/ref:.1f}% of ref)  within-q proj std {qcenter_mask((a5[:,S]*proj[S]).sum(1)[:,None],inA).std():.3f}\")\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":741,"cache_read_input_tokens":58465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":741},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6c1da5a-3bf1-4e9d-8966-f58382ed7a09","uuid":"b2a8f9d6-9a60-4a2d-8b55-d56ec61b168d","timestamp":"2026-11-13T13:31:13.806Z","request_id":"req_011Ch11SWkRM3B1x7AEWG9eG"}
